## Annex I — essential cybersecurity requirements

| Req | Provided by openmv-ota | Customer must add | Status |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1(2)(a) No known exploitable vulns at market | `build sbom` CycloneDX export + osv-scanner in CI (purl-identified components) | Track and act on findings; cover non-purl components until submodule purls land | ☐ |
| 1(2)(c) Updates throughout support period | ROMFS OTA mechanism | Commit to a support period | ☐ |
| 1(2)(d) Protection against unauthorised access | ECDSA (ES256/P-256) image signatures + anti-rollback + A/B fallback | — | ☐ |
| 1(2)(e) Confidentiality of stored data | **Out of scope** (no image encryption) | Add encryption if applicable | ☐ |
| 1(2)(f) Integrity of stored data | Signature + SHA-256 + CRC32 (ROMFS) | Cover /flash, /sdcard | ☐ |
| 1(2)(h) Availability of essential functions | Trial-boot + A/B fallback (single-image boards: firmware-resident recovery) | — | ☐ |
| 1(2)(j) Mitigate impact of incidents | Auto-rollback to the previous working release | — | ☐ |
| 1(2)(k) Security event recording | Hash-chained server audit log (all admin actions) | Device-side event recording in the app | ☐ |
| 1(2)(m) Vulnerability handling | OTA delivery + `build sbom` + disclosure/`security.txt` templates | Run the process | ☐ |

## Annex I — vulnerability handling

| Req | Provided | Customer must add | Status |
